# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project:
# Project Settings -> API -> Project URL and anon/public key.
#
# Leave both unset and the app runs off the catalog bundled in src/data/,
# which is the whole of the extracted library. Nothing breaks without them.
#
# The anon key is compiled into the bundle and is readable by anyone who opens
# the page. That is by design: it identifies the project, it does not authorise
# anything. Row level security in supabase/migrations/ decides what it can do,
# which is read the catalog and nothing else. Never put the service_role key
# in a VITE_ variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Sign in is by emailed link, and Supabase only redirects back to URLs it has
# been told about. In the dashboard, Authentication -> URL Configuration:
#   Site URL       http://localhost:3000
#   Redirect URLs  http://localhost:3000  (plus the deployed origin, if any)
# The dev server is pinned to port 3000 to match. Serve the app anywhere else
# and the emailed link lands on a port with nothing on it: the browser then
# says ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED even though the link itself was valid.
